<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_GreySeaFloorLife.xml             TerminalBiomes · authored 2026-09-26
  ============================================================================
  SEA_FISHABLES_ALIVE_IN_DEPTHS_1 — the GREY SEA portion — plus the Aerofleet
  replacement owed by GREYSEA_ANCHOR_CREATURES_1.

  Owner, at the bench 2026-09-26, typed:
      "All the fishables should also be alive and moving around in the depths
       (this is true for ALL seas)."

  ⇒ A catch item with nothing swimming is HALF a species. The Grey Sea
  shipped nine fishTypes rows against five floor residents; seven of the nine
  (sallik, karrud, hessal, oomal, maalu, immu, haarn) existed only as items.
  This file gives all seven a body.

  ============================================================================
  🔑 AUTHORED FROM THE CATCH ITEMS' OWN DESCRIPTIONS, NOT INVENTED
  ============================================================================
  The item item's own item text is the design. src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/
  Defs/ThingDefs_Items/RUT_GreySeaFish_Items.xml already describes a
  shell-less crab wearing its own excreted salt, a flat fish that gave up
  swimming and grows a mineral plate, a bivalve whose shells are grown from
  the sea's crystal, a blind sick brine-eel, a jelly half turned to stone, a
  soft thing that lodges in dead shells, and a walking mineral jacket nobody
  can identify. Every body size, speed, diet and behaviour flag below is read
  off those sentences. ⛔ Nothing here was made up; if a number looks odd,
  check the item text before "fixing" it.

  ============================================================================
  ✅ TIER: BOTH SIDES ARE NOW RM_ — GREYSEA_CATCH_TIER_RENAME_1, 2026-09-27
  ============================================================================
  The seven catch items shipped as RUT_Sallik etc. in the Utinni patch layer,
  MayRequire-gated on mandrake.rut.patches. Every one of those names is an
  INVENTED exotic word, not canon IP — and Q11a (biome_mod_architecture.md
  §7, owner 2026-09-22) rules that invented names are free-tier and belong in
  RM_: "the top mod without star wars will look precisely the same as the
  star wars enhanced one."

  The living counterparts below were already authored RM_ and cast INLINE on
  RM_GreySea with no MayRequire. The catch side has now caught up:
  RUT_Sallik/Karrud/Hessal/Oomal/Maalu/Immu/Haarn are renamed
  RM_SallikCatch/RM_KarrudCatch/RM_HessalCatch/RM_OomalCatch/RM_MaaluCatch/
  RM_ImmuCatch/RM_HaarnCatch, moved into this same mod's RM_GreySeaCatch.xml,
  so the pairing now reads RM_Sallik (floor) <-> RM_SallikCatch (catch),
  matching the RM_Essarn <-> RM_EssarnCatch shape. The free mod's Grey Sea
  is fully fishable on its own.

  RUT_RareGreyCatches (updated to reference RM_HessalCatch) and RUT_SaltCameo
  (unchanged) were out of that item's named scope and still carry their
  RUT_ defNames — a separate migration, not this one.

  ============================================================================
  EVERY ONE IS SOLITARY
  ============================================================================
  the_grey_deep.md ban 2 / terminator_sea.md §6: no herds, flocks, schools,
  packs or swarms; "anything that schools lives in the Twilight Deep." Every
  PawnKindDef here is wildGroupSize 1. No exceptions, and none may be added.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: flat texPaths under Things/Pawn/Animal/<defName>/, the
  posture RM_GreySeaFauna.xml established. Real art is owed via artpipe;
  search done/ and _artsrc/ by subject before queuing.
  ============================================================================
-->
