  <!-- ==================================================================
       RM_HAARN — "a jacket of pillar-mineral the size of a helmet,
       closed all round, that moves … from pillar to pillar, leaving a
       scrape-line in the silt like a very small version of the giant's
       … It is the Grey's only true extremophile: it lives in the
       strongest brine at the bottom, where nothing else survives."

       🔑 The scrape-line matters: the sheet's own always-true line is
       "fresh scrape-sign means the giant is near", and the haarn is
       that read at small scale — a false positive a diver learns. That
       is a fiction hook for a later scrape-sign mechanic, not a def
       field. Rarest of the seven (0.08) because it lives where nothing
       goes.
       ================================================================== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Haarn</defName>
    <label>haarn</label>
    <description>Nobody agrees what a haarn is. It is a jacket of pillar-mineral the size of a helmet, closed all round, and it moves — slowly, along the floor, pillar to pillar, leaving a scrape-line in the silt like a very small version of the giant's. Cut one open and there is a soft thing inside with no eyes and a great many small hooks, and it dies at once in open air. It lives in the strongest brine at the bottom, where nothing else survives, and it has plainly been doing so for a very long time.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>0.5</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>8</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>55</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Wildness>0.85</Wildness>
    </statBases>
